HOBBIT Units 1–2 patch: manifest schema v2 cold-expert parsing/storage and
cold slot runtime machinery. Unit 1's optional top-level `cold` object
contains `quant_type`, `source`, `family_bytes`, and optional per-layer
`layers` arrays of expert ids. Validation covers schema versions, type
capabilities, per-layer stride fit, layer/expert ranges, unique ids, JSON
shapes, and unsigned values above INT64_MAX before signed conversion.

Unit 3a adds cold tensor fields, cold load bases/views, and manifest suffix
resolution. Unit 2 adds only the const `llama_model::moe_experts_is_cold()`
forwarder plus the runtime cold binding/state, LRU allocation, direct cold
preadv installs, `llama_moe_slot_runtime::staged_cold_slot_ids()` accessor,
counters, and HOBBIT matmul-split rule.

LLAMA_MOE_HOBBIT is read once and defaults off; off leaves the hot runtime
path unchanged. In HOBBIT mode, each hot-prefill, hot-decode, cold-prefill,
and cold-decode binding set has exactly one zero slot. Cold tensor byte sizes
come only from the v2 cold family_bytes accessor; bytes_per_expert remains the
hot size. Cold prefill capacity is 128; cold decode views use each layer's hot
width. Empty v2 cold sets still allocate the full cold bank.

The runtime forces matmul_split to zero when HOBBIT is on, so no A2 install
is deferred. Cold experts remain in their manifest quantization and are read
directly into their own cold slot tensors; no conversion is performed.

Unit 3 adds `has_cold_layer()` and the chained `build_slot_ids_tensor_cold()`
operation (hot ids are both map_custom2 carriers; the callback ignores the
second source and copies the staged cold ids). When the runtime reports a
cold layer, build_moe_ffn computes separate hot and cold gate/up/activation/
down chains, then adds them immediately before router weighting. It rejects
fused gate_up, biases/scales, weight_before_ffn, and missing cold tensors with
named runtime errors. The hot graph names stay stock; the cold chain uses the
`_cold` names, and the add is `ffn_moe_dual_add`. MTP verification resolved:
this trial GGUF has nextn_predict_layers absent/default zero, so no MTP graph
block exists and the reverse-gap guard is inert for graph_mtp.

